 "version": "1.0.0",
 "description": "Kerala colloquial clinical semantics. Maps what a patient/doctor MEANT to canonical clinical concepts. This is NOT an ASR-correction table (see asr_corrections evidence in scribe_engine/asr_correction.py) and NOT a symptom alias list (that lives in malayalam_clinical_lexicon.json). Every mapping here is context-aware: high/low/check/ask/family are distinguished before any finding is made.",
 "notes": [
  "controlled_targets are chronic-condition concepts whose colloquial names double as measurements: 'pressure' can mean the disease, a high value, a low value, a check-up request, or a question about the reading. Each must resolve differently.",
  "A low marker (കുറവാണ്/low) on a controlled target MUST NOT produce the disease: it produces the derived low concept (hypotension / hypoglycemia).",
  "A measurement/check marker (നോക്കണം/check/അളക്കണം) is a request for a reading, never a diagnosis.",
  "An amount question (എത്രയാണ്/how much) is a question about a reading, never a diagnosis.",
  "A control marker (control ആണ്/normal) means the chronic condition is PRESENT but controlled. Never downgrade to ABSENT: a controlled chronic condition is still a chronic condition.",
  "Family subjects (അമ്മ/അച്ഛൻ/കുടുംബം) make the mention family history. Never a patient finding.",
  "Colloquial symptom aliases marked here are merged into the base lexicon at load time; the base scope engine (negation/question/temporality) applies to them unchanged.",
  "Anything not confidently mapped is left alone: UNKNOWN beats GUESS."
 ],
